;; Running furniture: headers, footers and page numbers (P4.3; SPEC 10.2; D017, D034, D076, D173-D176). emon's own module (D039).
;;
;;   (fu-find wd ln et gl mk pages npages txt md lb trust mode  cd sl gr ord tx bh fo fp ft pl)
;;                         BEFORE the paragraph stage: find the furniture, take its lines OUT of `ln` (so P1.8's
;;                         paragraphs, and P4.1's gutters after them, never see it), and write what was decided into the
;;                         work arenas
;;   (fu-write fo fp ft pl npages nodes attrs regions text pages ledger)
;;                         AFTER it: the page labels, the dropped-items ledger, the `furniture` roots, and the `label`
;;                         of every page milestone, into the Model
;;
;; THE RULE (SPEC 10.2, D017): drop what the output already says; keep once what is the same on every page; keep per page
;; what varies; turn page numbers into page labels. The maintainer's form: a page number, running header or footer is
;; dropped only when it is just page numbering and a title; anything else is KEPT (as an aside), so "Case 1:21-cv-00123
;; Filed 05/03/21", "CONFIDENTIAL" and a Bates number survive, and a ledger row says what was dropped and why.
;;
;; THE EVIDENCE, in the order it is used (every one is a signal, none is believed alone: D034):
;;   1. POSITION. A candidate is an upright line whose centre is in the top or bottom 11 % of the page, or a sideways one in
;;      the outer 12 % of its width (a margin stamp). The text layer's `lines` already split a header's left, centre and
;;      right parts, so each is a candidate of its own.
;;   2. RECURRENCE ON A TEMPLATE. The text with every digit run abstracted (`#`) and every roman-numeral page number
;;      abstracted (`$`), hashed (64 bits), grouped by (zone, hash) and then by vertical position (a chain within 1.5 % of
;;      the page's height). `Page 3 of 10` and `Page 4 of 10` are one template; `ACME-01` and `ACME-02` are one. The
;;      group is analysed SLOT by slot (a slot is one abstracted number): a slot that is the same on every page is a
;;      CONSTANT (`of 10`, `2024`), one that rises by exactly the page step from one member to the next is the PAGE NUMBER
;;      (`3`, `iii`; at least 3 of 4 pairs), anything else VARIES (a Bates number that skips). A page number is a whole
;;      token, so `ACME-01` is an identifier, not a page number: its slot is EMBEDDED, and when it equals the page index
;;      the template says `ACME-{n:02}` (the same spelling the gold uses: `{n}` the page, `{n:0W}` zero-padded).
;;   3. ISOLATION. A running header is set apart from the body: the next line toward the page's inside is at least half a line
;;      away, counting only lines that do not themselves recur. A table's repeated header row is not: it is followed at once
;;      by its first row. (A pure page number is exempt: it needs no isolation.)
;;   4. THE TAGGED TREE (P3.7, D076). A line whose glyphs are /Artifact marked content is evidence FOR (Pagination, or a Header
;;      in the top zone, or a Footer in the bottom zone: an artifact in the wrong place is ignored), a line inside tagged
;;      content is evidence AGAINST, and each counts for `trust` (the informativeness score of the tree, 0..1000) per
;;      mille: `score = recurrence + 0.6 x trust x (artifact share - content share)`, 600 to qualify.
;;      Recurrence is 300 for one page, 500 + 150 x pages (at most 1000) for two or more.
;;   5. COVERAGE. A recurring template covers at least 30 % of the pages (a page-number template at least 3 pages), or the
;;      tree says so. A line seen on two of fifty pages is not furniture.
;;   6. STYLE AND POSITION (a header whose text changes: a chapter title, an odd/even pair). Lines in the tighter top and
;;      bottom 8.5 % bands, with the same size (to 0.5 pt) and the same vertical position, on at least 60 % of the pages,
;;      isolated on 70 % of them, no larger than the body text (the most common line size outside the bands, plus 3 %):
;;      furniture whose text varies, kept per page.
;;
;; DECOMPOSITION (SPEC 10.2 step 2). The tokens of a template minus the PAGE SLOT, the page words (`Page`, `Seite`, `de`, ...)
;; and the total after an "of" word, minus punctuation-only tokens, is what REMAINS. Nothing remains: a page number, DROPPED
;; (`page-number`) and its number kept as the page's label. Something remains and it is the document's title (the Info
;; /Title) or the text of a line of the body, or of two or three consecutive lines (a title that wraps, a heading that the
;; running section title repeats), compared by letters and digits only, 64-bit hashes, at least 4 characters: it is already
;; in the output, DROPPED (`running-title`). Anything else is KEPT: ONE `furniture` root when the same on every page (its
;; template and pages), one per page when it varies. The page number part of a mixed line is still the page's label.
;;
;; PAGE LABELS (SPEC 3.7). /PageLabels (P3.9) wins when the catalogue has it; otherwise the printed number (as printed:
;; `iii`, `03`) of the best page-number group. A page with neither has none; none is inferred.
;;
;; THE POLICY SETTING (SPEC 13, `furniture: drop|keep|policy`): `mode` 0 policy (above), 1 keep (nothing leaves the flow; the
;; labels still come out), 2 drop (every furniture group leaves the flow and nothing is kept: the ledger says what).
;;
;; WHAT IT DOES NOT DO: visibility (P3.5/P3.6) and watermarks; the page number of a line that is part of a longer
;; paragraph; the language of a page-number word beyond the table below; a number written in words.
(ns emon.furniture
  (:require [emon.lang :refer [I32 I64 Cells i64 i32 mul64 shr64 defenum]]
            [emon.port :refer [cells-len cells-at cells-set cells-push cells-drop]]
            [emon.evidence :refer [wd-get ln-get ln-set ln-count lh-page lh-x0 lh-y0 lh-x1 lh-y1 lh-rot
                                   lh-first lh-count hd-tstart hd-tlen wf-size wf-gfirst wf-gcount gf-mark
                                   gl-get mk-get mk-artifact-of mkf-mcid mkf-parent]]
            [emon.model :refer [node-new node-set-text node-set-sub node-set-conf node-add-src node-add-region
                                node-count node-kind node-sub page-count node-set-attr-text node-add-attr-int
                                page-new page-w page-h page-set-label page-label-start page-label-len
                                ledger-add ledger-set-text text-append-cp
                                nk-furniture nk-break fk-label fk-pages sr-text sr-struct sr-infer
                                dr-page-number dr-running-title dr-watermark rl-header rl-footer rl-margin]]
            [emon.normalize :refer [nz-nfc nz-flag-ligatures nz-flag-radicals]]
            [emon.pdfmeta :refer [pm-label-cells]]
            [kin.lang :refer [defn defconst defdata return let set while if do comment
                              + - * < > <= >= == != and or quot rem bit-xor]]))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- the knobs
;; Every threshold is here, named, in per mille or in the unit it judges. First values: P10.1 calibrates them.
(defconst ^I32 FU_TOP 110)          ;; top zone: the line's centre is above this per mille of the page's height
(defconst ^I32 FU_BOT 890)          ;; bottom zone: below this
(defconst ^I32 FU_SIDE 120)         ;; margin zone: a sideways line's centre is within this per mille of the width of an edge
(defconst ^I32 FU_STOP 85)          ;; the tighter bands of the style rule (6)
(defconst ^I32 FU_SBOT 915)
(defconst ^I32 FU_YTOL 15)          ;; vertical position tolerance, per mille of the page's height
(defconst ^I32 FU_MAXLEN 160)       ;; a longer line is a sentence, not furniture
(defconst ^I32 FU_SPCLEN 100)       ;; and for the style rule
(defconst ^I32 FU_COVER 30)         ;; per cent of the pages a recurring template must cover
(defconst ^I32 FU_SCOVER 60)        ;; per cent, the style rule
(defconst ^I32 FU_ISOGAP 1500)       ;; isolation: the gap to the next line toward the inside, per mille of the line's height (a text group)
(defconst ^I32 FU_SISOGAP 2000)      ;; the same for the style rule
(defconst ^I32 FU_ISOPCT 60)           ;; per cent of a group's members that must be isolated
(defconst ^I32 FU_SISO 70)          ;; the style rule
(defconst ^I32 FU_QUAL 600)         ;; the score to qualify
(defconst ^I32 FU_TAGW 6)           ;; tenths of the trust that the tag evidence is worth
(defconst ^I32 FU_PAIRS 75)         ;; per cent of consecutive pairs that must step with the page for a slot to be the page number
(defconst ^I32 FU_MINNORM 4)        ;; characters (letters and digits) a title match needs
(defconst ^I32 FU_MAXSLOTS 8)
(defconst ^I32 FU_FLOOR 3600)       ;; a margin zone is at least this deep (centipoints: 36 pt) on a short page (D1630) ...
(defconst ^I32 FU_FCAP 170)         ;; ... and never deeper than this per mille of the page's height
(defconst ^I32 FU_STAMP 60)         ;; a sideways line this near a side edge (per mille of the width, centre) is a margin stamp (D1630) ...
(defconst ^I32 FU_STAMPLEN 8)       ;; ... of at least this many characters
(defconst ^I32 FU_CELLS 4)         ;; a row of this many candidates or more on one baseline is a table's row, not a running header (D1630)
(defconst ^I32 FU_CHAIN_GAP 1300)   ;; a line this close under (per mille of its height) a header line that qualified goes with it (D1630)

;; the work arenas' strides (documented where each is made)
(defconst ^I32 CD 16)
(defconst ^I32 SL 10)
(defconst ^I32 GR 16)
(defconst ^I32 FO 12)
(defconst ^I32 FP 5)

;; `md` (emon.pdfmeta's header): 2 the Info /Title as a run in `txt`, 54 the number of page label ranges.
(defconst ^I32 FU_MD_TITLE 2)
(defconst ^I32 FU_MD_RANGES 54)

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the tables
;; Page words and "of" words (flag 1 page word, 2 "of" word; each a run of lowercase code points ended by 0; -1 ends the table).
(defdata ^:pub fu-pw
  :emitter kin.lang/flat-array
  :data [1 112 97 103 101 0 1 112 97 103 101 115 0 1 112 97 103 0 1 112 97 103 105 110 97 0 1 112 225 103 105 110 97 0 1 112 103 0 1 112 112 0 1 112 0 1 115 101 105 116 101 0 1 115 0 1 115 105 100 97 0 1 115 116 114 111 110 97 0 1 115 116 114 0 1 115 105 100 101 0 1 102 111 108 105 111 0 1 98 108 97 116 116 0 2 111 102 0 2 100 101 0 2 118 111 110 0 2 115 117 114 0 2 100 105 0 2 100 117 0 2 118 97 110 0 2 97 118 0 2 122 0 -1]
  :accessors {^I32 fu-pw-at [^I32 ignored ^I32 i]})

;; Caption words (a line that begins with one is a caption, never a running header): lowercase, each ended by 0, -1 ends.
(defdata ^:pub fu-cw
  :emitter kin.lang/flat-array
  :data [116 97 98 108 101 0 102 105 103 117 114 101 0 102 105 103 0 99 104 97 114 116 0 101 120 104 105 98 105 116 0 103 114 97 112 104 0 116 97 98 101 108 108 101 0 97 98 98 105 108 100 117 110 103 0 116 97 98 108 101 97 117 0 102 105 103 117 114 97 0 116 97 98 108 97 0 116 97 98 101 108 108 97 0 99 117 97 100 114 111 0 103 114 225 102 105 99 111 0 103 114 97 102 105 99 111 0 112 108 97 116 101 0 115 99 104 101 109 101 0 108 105 115 116 105 110 103 0 98 111 120 0 109 97 112 0 -1]
  :accessors {^I32 fu-cw-at [^I32 ignored ^I32 i]})

;; The roman numeral table: value, first symbol, second symbol (0: none), greedily from the largest.
(defdata ^:pub fu-rn
  :emitter kin.lang/flat-array
  :data [1000 77 0 900 67 77 500 68 0 400 67 68 100 67 0 90 88 67 50 76 0 40 88 76 10 88 0 9 73 88 5 86 0 4 73 86 1 73 0]
  :accessors {^I32 fu-rn-at [^I32 ignored ^I32 i]})

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ small things
(defn ^I32 fu-min [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (if (< a b) (return a))
  (return b))

(defn ^I32 fu-max [^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (if (> a b) (return a))
  (return b))

(defn ^I32 fu-abs [^I32 a]
  (if (< a 0) (return (- 0 a)))
  (return a))

(defn ^I32 cd-get [^Cells cd ^I32 r ^I32 f] (return (cells-at cd (+ (* r 16) f))))
(defn ^I32 cd-set [^:mut ^Cells cd ^I32 r ^I32 f ^I32 v]
  (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) f) v)
  (return 0))
(defn ^I32 sl-get [^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 f] (return (cells-at sl (+ (* r 10) f))))
(defn ^I32 gr-get [^Cells gr ^I32 r ^I32 f] (return (cells-at gr (+ (* r 16) f))))
(defn ^I32 gr-set [^:mut ^Cells gr ^I32 r ^I32 f ^I32 v]
  (cells-set gr (+ (* r 16) f) v)
  (return 0))
(defn ^I32 gr-inc [^:mut ^Cells gr ^I32 r ^I32 f]
  (let [^I32 v (gr-get gr r f)]
    (gr-set gr r f (+ v 1))
    (return 0)))
(defn ^I32 fo-get [^Cells fo ^I32 r ^I32 f] (return (cells-at fo (+ (* r 12) f))))

(defn ^I32 fu-push-row [^:mut ^Cells c ^I32 stride]
  (comment "Append a row of zeros; answer its index.")
  (let [^I32 r (quot (cells-len c) stride)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0]
    (while (< i stride)
      (do (cells-push c 0)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return r)))

(defn ^I32 fu-digit [^I32 c]
  (if (and (>= c 48) (<= c 57)) (return 1))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 fu-lower [^I32 c]
  (if (and (>= c 65) (<= c 90)) (return (+ c 32)))
  (if (and (>= c 192) (and (<= c 222) (!= c 215))) (return (+ c 32)))
  (return c))

(defn ^I32 fu-alnum [^I32 c]
  (comment "A letter or a digit, for the comparison of titles: ASCII, and everything from U+00C0 up except the general")
  (comment "punctuation, arrows and symbols (U+2000..2BFF), the CJK and full-width punctuation.")
  (if (and (>= c 48) (<= c 57)) (return 1))
  (if (and (>= c 65) (<= c 90)) (return 1))
  (if (and (>= c 97) (<= c 122)) (return 1))
  (if (< c 192) (return 0))
  (if (== c 215) (return 0))
  (if (== c 247) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= c 8192) (<= c 11263)) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= c 12288) (<= c 12351)) (return 0))
  (if (and (>= c 65280) (<= c 65295)) (return 0))
  (return 1))

(defn ^I32 fu-punct [^I32 c]
  (comment "A character that is stripped from both ends of a token to find its core: brackets, quotes, dashes, bullets,")
  (comment "stops and slashes.")
  (if (and (>= c 40) (<= c 47))
    (if (!= c 43) (return 1)))
  (if (or (== c 33) (or (== c 34) (or (== c 39) (or (== c 58) (or (== c 59) (or (== c 60) (or (== c 62) (or (== c 63) (or (== c 91) (or (== c 92) (or (== c 93) (or (== c 95) (or (== c 123) (or (== c 124) (or (== c 125) (== c 126)))))))))))))))) (return 1))
  (if (or (== c 183) (or (== c 171) (== c 187))) (return 1))
  (if (and (>= c 8208) (<= c 8213)) (return 1))
  (if (or (== c 8216) (or (== c 8217) (or (== c 8220) (or (== c 8221) (or (== c 8226) (or (== c 8249) (== c 8250))))))) (return 1))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I64 fu-step [^I64 h ^I32 c]
  (comment "One step of a 64-bit FNV-1a over code points.")
  (return (mul64 (bit-xor h (i64 c)) 1099511628211)))

(defn ^I64 fu-basis []
  (return -3750763034362895579))

;; --------------------------------------------------------------- roman numerals
(defn ^I32 fu-upper [^I32 c]
  (if (and (>= c 97) (<= c 122)) (return (- c 32)))
  (return c))

(defn ^I32 fu-roman-sym [^I32 c]
  (comment "The value of a roman symbol of either case, 0 for anything else.")
  (let [^I32 u (fu-upper c)]
    (if (== u 73) (return 1))
    (if (== u 86) (return 5))
    (if (== u 88) (return 10))
    (if (== u 76) (return 50))
    (if (== u 67) (return 100))
    (if (== u 68) (return 500))
    (if (== u 77) (return 1000))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-roman-val [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 ce]
  (comment "The value of tx[cs, ce) read as a roman numeral of one case, in its canonical spelling and at most 3999; -1")
  (comment "for anything else (so `mim`, `iiii` and `vx` are not numerals).")
  (let [^I32 n (- ce cs)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 total 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 up 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lo 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0]
    (if (or (< n 1) (> n 15)) (return -1))
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set c (cells-at tx (+ cs i)))
          (if (== (fu-roman-sym c) 0) (return -1))
          (if (and (>= c 65) (<= c 90)) (set up 1) (set lo 1))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (and (== up 1) (== lo 1)) (return -1))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set v (fu-roman-sym (cells-at tx (+ cs i))))
          (set nx 0)
          (if (< (+ i 1) n) (set nx (fu-roman-sym (cells-at tx (+ cs (+ i 1))))))
          (if (< v nx)
            (set total (- total v))
            (set total (+ total v)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (or (< total 1) (> total 3999)) (return -1))
    ;; canonical: regenerate the numeral greedily and compare symbol by symbol
    (let [^:mut ^I32 left total
          ^:mut ^I32 pos 0
          ^:mut ^I32 k 0
          ^:mut ^I32 s1 0
          ^:mut ^I32 s2 0
          ^:mut ^I32 cc 0]
      (while (< k 39)
        (do (set s1 (fu-rn-at 0 (+ k 1)))
            (set s2 (fu-rn-at 0 (+ k 2)))
            (while (>= left (fu-rn-at 0 k))
              (do (if (>= pos n) (return -1))
                  (set cc (fu-upper (cells-at tx (+ cs pos))))
                  (if (!= cc s1) (return -1))
                  (set pos (+ pos 1))
                  (if (> s2 0)
                    (do (if (>= pos n) (return -1))
                        (set cc (fu-upper (cells-at tx (+ cs pos))))
                        (if (!= cc s2) (return -1))
                        (set pos (+ pos 1))))
                  (set left (- left (fu-rn-at 0 k)))))
            (set k (+ k 3))))
      (if (!= pos n) (return -1))
      (return total))))

;; --------------------------------------------------------------- tokens
(defn ^I32 fu-cs [^Cells tx ^I32 s ^I32 e]
  (comment "The start of the core of the token tx[s, e): past the punctuation at its front.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i s]
    (while (and (< i e) (== (fu-punct (cells-at tx i)) 1))
      (set i (+ i 1)))
    (return i)))

(defn ^I32 fu-ce [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 e]
  (comment "The end of the core (exclusive): before the punctuation at the back; never before `cs`.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i e]
    (while (and (> i cs) (== (fu-punct (cells-at tx (- i 1))) 1))
      (set i (- i 1)))
    (return i)))

(defn ^I32 fu-pw-kind [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 ce]
  (comment "0 for a core that is no page word, 1 for a page word (`Page`, `Seite`, `p`), 2 for an \"of\" word (`of`, `de`, `von`).")
  (let [^I32 n (- ce cs)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 flag 0
        ^:mut ^I32 wl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ok 1
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (if (< n 1) (return 0))
    (while (>= (fu-pw-at 0 i) 0)
      (do (set flag (fu-pw-at 0 i))
          (set i (+ i 1))
          (set wl 0)
          (while (!= (fu-pw-at 0 (+ i wl)) 0)
            (set wl (+ wl 1)))
          (if (== wl n)
            (do (set ok 1)
                (set j 0)
                (while (< j n)
                  (do (if (!= (fu-lower (cells-at tx (+ cs j))) (fu-pw-at 0 (+ i j))) (set ok 0))
                      (set j (+ j 1))))
                (if (== ok 1) (return flag))))
          (set i (+ i (+ wl 1)))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-caption-lead [^Cells tx ^Cells cd ^I32 r]
  (comment "1 when the candidate's text begins with a caption word (`Table 3.`, `Figure 2`, `Abbildung`): a caption is content, not")
  (comment "a running header, whatever its position.")
  (let [^I32 bs (cd-get cd r 11)
        ^I32 end (+ bs (cd-get cd r 12))
        ^:mut ^I32 e bs
        ^:mut ^I32 cs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ce 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 wl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ok 1
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
      (set e (+ e 1)))
    (set cs (fu-cs tx bs e))
    (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
    (if (>= cs ce) (return 0))
    (while (>= (fu-cw-at 0 i) 0)
      (do (set wl 0)
          (while (!= (fu-cw-at 0 (+ i wl)) 0)
            (set wl (+ wl 1)))
          (if (== wl (- ce cs))
            (do (set ok 1)
                (set j 0)
                (while (< j wl)
                  (do (if (!= (fu-lower (cells-at tx (+ cs j))) (fu-cw-at 0 (+ i j))) (set ok 0))
                      (set j (+ j 1))))
                (if (== ok 1) (return 1))))
          (set i (+ i (+ wl 1)))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-numeric [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 ce]
  (comment "1 when the core is digits, and slashes between digit runs of at most nine digits: `3`, `03`, `3/10`.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i cs
        ^:mut ^I32 run 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0]
    (if (>= cs ce) (return 0))
    (while (< i ce)
      (do (set c (cells-at tx i))
          (if (== (fu-digit c) 1)
            (set run (+ run 1))
            (do (if (!= c 47) (return 0))
                (if (== run 0) (return 0))
                (set run 0)))
          (if (> run 9) (return 0))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (== run 0) (return 0))
    (return 1)))

;; token classes: 0 nothing but punctuation, 1 page word, 2 "of" word, 3 numeric, 4 roman numeral, 5 anything else
(defn ^I32 fu-tclass [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 ce]
  (if (>= cs ce) (return 0))
  (let [^I32 pk (fu-pw-kind tx cs ce)]
    (if (> pk 0) (return pk)))
  (if (== (fu-numeric tx cs ce) 1) (return 3))
  (if (> (fu-roman-val tx cs ce) 0) (return 4))
  (return 5))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------- a candidate's text and slots
;; cd (candidate rows, CD = 16): 0 line, 1 page (1-based), 2 zone (1 top, 2 bottom, 3 margin), 3 y0, 4 y1, 5 template hash low,
;; 6 template hash high, 7 slots (-1: too many, never grouped), 8 group, 9 tag state (0 none, 1 artifact in place,
;; 2 tagged content, 3 artifact out of place), 10 isolated (0/1), 11 text start in `tx`, 12 text length, 13 first slot row in `sl`,
;; 14 size of the first word, 15 state (0 free, 1 member of a qualified template group, 2 of a qualified style group).
;; sl (slot rows, SL = 10): 0 candidate row, 1 kind (1 a number token, 2 a roman numeral token, 3 digits inside another
;; token), 2 value (-1 unknown), 3 start of the digit run or the numeral in the line's text, 4 its length, 5 token ordinal,
;; 6 digits (0 for a numeral), 7 1 for an upper-case numeral, 8 the token's start in the line's text, 9 its length.

(defn ^I32 fu-line-text [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^:mut ^Cells out ^I32 l]
  (comment "The line's words joined by one space, appended to `out`; answers the length.")
  (let [^I32 w0 (ln-get ln l (lh-first))
        ^I32 wn (ln-get ln l (lh-count))
        ^I32 start (cells-len out)
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 started 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0]
    (while (< k wn)
      (do (set ts (wd-get wd (+ w0 k) (hd-tstart)))
          (set tl (wd-get wd (+ w0 k) (hd-tlen)))
          (if (and (>= ts 0) (> tl 0))
            (do (if (== started 1) (cells-push out 32))
                (set started 1)
                (set j 0)
                (while (< j tl)
                  (do (cells-push out (cells-at et (+ ts j)))
                      (set j (+ j 1))))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (return (- (cells-len out) start))))

(defn ^I32 fu-slot-push [^:mut ^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 kind ^I32 value ^I32 ds ^I32 dl ^I32 tok ^I32 nd ^I32 up ^I32 ts ^I32 tl]
  (let [^I32 s (fu-push-row sl 10)]
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 0) r)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 1) kind)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 2) value)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 3) ds)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 4) dl)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 5) tok)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 6) nd)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 7) up)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 8) ts)
    (cells-set sl (+ (* s 10) 9) tl)
    (return s)))

(defn ^I32 fu-prefixed [^Cells tx ^I32 cs ^I32 ce]
  (comment "The start of the digits of a core that is one or two letters, perhaps a `-` or a `.`, and at most nine digits (`K-1`,")
  (comment "`A-12`, `F3`): a page number of a part of a document (SPEC 10.2); -1 for any other core. `ACME-01` is an identifier.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i cs
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0]
    (while (and (< i ce) (and (< (- i cs) 3) (or (and (>= (cells-at tx i) 65) (<= (cells-at tx i) 90)) (and (>= (cells-at tx i) 97) (<= (cells-at tx i) 122)))))
      (set i (+ i 1)))
    (if (or (< (- i cs) 1) (> (- i cs) 2)) (return -1))
    (if (>= i ce) (return -1))
    (set c (cells-at tx i))
    (if (or (== c 45) (or (== c 46) (== c 8211))) (set i (+ i 1)))
    (if (>= i ce) (return -1))
    (if (> (- ce i) 9) (return -1))
    (set c i)
    (while (< c ce)
      (do (if (== (fu-digit (cells-at tx c)) 0) (return -1))
          (set c (+ c 1))))
    (return i)))

(defn ^I32 fu-slots [^Cells tx ^I32 bs ^I32 n ^:mut ^Cells sl ^:mut ^Cells cd ^I32 r]
  (comment "Tokenise the candidate's text tx[bs, bs+n): find its number slots (pushed on `sl`), and its template hash.")
  (comment "A roman numeral is a slot only when every token of the line is a page word, an \"of\" word, a number or a numeral")
  (comment "(`iv`, `Page iv`, `- IV -`): a numeral is otherwise a word (`mix`, `did`, `I`).")
  (let [^I32 end (+ bs n)
        ^:mut ^I32 i bs
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ce 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 d 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pageish 1
        ^:mut ^I32 ns 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pf -1
        ^:mut ^I32 kind1 3
        ^:mut ^I32 over 0
        ^:mut ^I64 h (fu-basis)]
    (while (< i end)
      (if (== (cells-at tx i) 32)
        (set i (+ i 1))
        (do (set e i)
            (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
              (set e (+ e 1)))
            (set cs (fu-cs tx i e))
            (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
            (if (== (fu-tclass tx cs ce) 5) (set pageish 0))
            (set i e))))
    (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) 13) (quot (cells-len sl) 10))
    (set i bs)
    (while (< i end)
      (if (== (cells-at tx i) 32)
        (do (set h (fu-step h 32))
            (set i (+ i 1)))
        (do (set e i)
            (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
              (set e (+ e 1)))
            (set cs (fu-cs tx i e))
            (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
            (set k (fu-tclass tx cs ce))
            (set pf -1)
            (if (== k 5) (set pf (fu-prefixed tx cs ce)))
            (set j i)
            (while (< j cs)
              (do (set h (fu-step h (cells-at tx j)))
                  (set j (+ j 1))))
            (if (and (== k 4) (== pageish 1))
              (do (if (< ns FU_MAXSLOTS)
                    (do (let [^:mut ^I32 up 0]
                          (if (and (>= (cells-at tx cs) 65) (<= (cells-at tx cs) 90)) (set up 1))
                          (fu-slot-push sl r 2 (fu-roman-val tx cs ce) (- cs bs) (- ce cs) tok 0 up (- i bs) (- e i)))
                        (set ns (+ ns 1)))
                    (set over 1))
                  (set h (fu-step h 36)))
              (do (set j cs)
                  (while (< j ce)
                    (do (set c (cells-at tx j))
                        (if (== (fu-digit c) 1)
                          (do (set d j)
                              (set v 0)
                              (while (and (< d ce) (== (fu-digit (cells-at tx d)) 1))
                                (do (if (< (- d j) 9) (set v (+ (* v 10) (- (cells-at tx d) 48))))
                                    (set d (+ d 1))))
                              (if (> (- d j) 9) (set v -1))
                              (set kind1 3)
                              (if (== k 3) (set kind1 1))
                              (if (< ns FU_MAXSLOTS)
                                (do (if (== j pf)
                                      (fu-slot-push sl r 4 v (- cs bs) (- ce cs) tok (- d j) 0 (- i bs) (- e i))
                                      (fu-slot-push sl r kind1 v (- j bs) (- d j) tok (- d j) 0 (- i bs) (- e i)))
                                    (set ns (+ ns 1)))
                                (set over 1))
                              (set h (fu-step h 35))
                              (set j d))
                          (do (set h (fu-step h c))
                              (set j (+ j 1))))))))
            (set j ce)
            (while (< j e)
              (do (set h (fu-step h (cells-at tx j)))
                  (set j (+ j 1))))
            (set tok (+ tok 1))
            (set i e))))
    (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) 5) (i32 h))
    (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) 6) (i32 (shr64 h 32)))
    (if (== over 1)
      (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) 7) -1)
      (cells-set cd (+ (* r 16) 7) ns))
    (return ns)))

(defn ^I32 fu-tag [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells gl ^Cells mk ^I32 l ^I32 zone]
  (comment "What the tagged PDF says about the line (SPEC 8.4.3, D076): by the marked content of its words' first glyphs,")
  (comment "the share that is an /Artifact in its place (1: Pagination; Header in the top zone; Footer in the bottom zone), an")
  (comment "/Artifact out of place (3), or inside a marked content with an MCID (2). 0 when no share reaches 60 %.")
  (let [^I32 w0 (ln-get ln l (lh-first))
        ^I32 wn (ln-get ln l (lh-count))
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 sup 0
        ^:mut ^I32 oth 0
        ^:mut ^I32 con 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ty 0
        ^:mut ^I32 su 0]
    (while (< k wn)
      (do (set g (wd-get wd (+ w0 k) (wf-gfirst)))
          (if (and (>= g 0) (> (wd-get wd (+ w0 k) (wf-gcount)) 0))
            (do (set tot (+ tot 1))
                (set m (gl-get gl g (gf-mark)))
                (if (>= m 0)
                  (do (set a (mk-artifact-of mk m))
                      (if (> a 0)
                        (do (set ty (quot a 16))
                            (set su (rem a 16))
                            (if (or (== ty 1) (or (and (== su 1) (== zone 1)) (and (== su 2) (== zone 2))))
                              (set sup (+ sup 1))
                              (set oth (+ oth 1))))
                        (do (set t m)
                            (while (>= t 0)
                              (do (if (>= (mk-get mk t (mkf-mcid)) 0)
                                    (do (set con (+ con 1))
                                        (set t -1))
                                    (set t (mk-get mk t (mkf-parent))))))))))))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (if (== tot 0) (return 0))
    (if (>= (* sup 10) (* tot 6)) (return 1))
    (if (>= (* oth 10) (* tot 6)) (return 3))
    (if (>= (* con 10) (* tot 6)) (return 2))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-zone-floor [^I32 h]
  (comment "D1630 (smoke review B issue 11): twice the depth (centipoints) of the margin zones of a page `h` tall when 11 per cent of it is less than FU_FLOOR (36 pt) and 17 per cent of it more")
  (comment "than 11 per cent: a page the size of a slide or a small card (210 pt tall) has a running header 18 pt from its top edge and a footer 28 pt from its foot, outside 11 per cent")
  (comment "of it. 0 for a page where 11 per cent is deep enough (every page of a letter's size and over 327 pt tall).")
  (let [^I32 lim (fu-min (* 2 FU_FLOOR) (quot (* h FU_FCAP) 500))]
    (if (> lim (quot (* h FU_TOP) 500)) (return lim))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-row-cells [^Cells ln ^I32 l]
  (comment "D1630 (smoke review A issue 15): how many upright lines (this one included) of its page stand on line l's baseline (centres within half its height), among the 40 lines either side of it")
  (comment "in the text layer's order. A row of FU_CELLS or more is a table's row, not a running header or footer (a left, a centre and a right part at the most): the first data row of a")
  (comment "continuation page, directly under the repeated header, recurs by position and by the shape of its cells and passed as a header that varies.")
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^I32 c2 (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)))
        ^I32 half (fu-max 1 (- (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y0))))
        ^I32 p (ln-get ln l (lh-page))
        ^:mut ^I32 q (fu-max 0 (- l 40))
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0]
    (while (and (< q nl) (<= q (+ l 40)))
      (do (set rot (ln-get ln q (lh-rot)))
          (if (and (== (ln-get ln q (lh-page)) p)
                   (and (or (< rot 100) (> rot 35900))
                        (<= (fu-abs (- (+ (ln-get ln q (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln q (lh-y1))) c2)) half)))
            (set n (+ n 1)))
          (set q (+ q 1))))
    (return n)))

(defn ^I32 fu-scan [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^Cells gl ^Cells mk ^Cells pages ^I32 npages
                    ^:mut ^Cells cd ^:mut ^Cells sl ^:mut ^Cells tx]
  (comment "Every candidate line of the document as a row of `cd`, in line order. Answers the number of rows, or -1 when the")
  (comment "lines are not in page order (nothing here is then safe to say).")
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prev 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 zone 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cy2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0]
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (set p (ln-get ln l (lh-page)))
          (if (< p prev) (return -1))
          (if (> p prev) (set prev p))
          (if (and (>= p 1) (<= p npages))
            (do (set w (page-w pages (- p 1)))
                (set h (page-h pages (- p 1)))
                (set rot (ln-get ln l (lh-rot)))
                (set zone 0)
                (set cy2 (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y1))))
                (set cx2 (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-x1))))
                (if (or (< rot 100) (> rot 35900))
                  (do (let [^I32 fz (fu-zone-floor h)]
                        (if (< cy2 (fu-max fz (quot (* h FU_TOP) 500))) (set zone 1))
                        (if (> fz 0)
                          (if (> cy2 (- (* 2 h) fz)) (set zone 2))
                          (if (> cy2 (quot (* h FU_BOT) 500)) (set zone 2)))))
                  (if (or (< (fu-abs (- rot 9000)) 100) (< (fu-abs (- rot 27000)) 100))
                    (if (or (< cx2 (quot (* w FU_SIDE) 500)) (> cx2 (quot (* w (- 1000 FU_SIDE)) 500)))
                      (set zone 3))))
                (if (and (> zone 0) (< zone 3) (>= (fu-row-cells ln l) FU_CELLS)) (set zone 0))
                (if (> zone 0)
                  (do (set ts (cells-len tx))
                      (set tl (fu-line-text wd ln et tx l))
                      (if (or (== tl 0) (> tl FU_MAXLEN))
                        (cells-drop tx ts)
                        (do (set r (fu-push-row cd 16))
                            (cd-set cd r 0 l)
                            (cd-set cd r 1 p)
                            (cd-set cd r 2 zone)
                            (cd-set cd r 3 (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)))
                            (cd-set cd r 4 (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)))
                            (cd-set cd r 8 -1)
                            (cd-set cd r 11 ts)
                            (cd-set cd r 12 tl)
                            (fu-slots tx ts tl sl cd r)
                            (cd-set cd r 9 (fu-tag wd ln gl mk l zone))
                            (let [^I32 w0 (ln-get ln l (lh-first))]
                              (cd-set cd r 14 (wd-get wd w0 (wf-size))))))))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (return (quot (cells-len cd) 16))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------- groups
;; The sort keys. mode 0: (zone, hash high, hash low, y0, page): the template groups. mode 1: (group, page): a group's
;; members in page order. mode 2: (zone, size in half points, y0, page): the style groups.
(defn ^I32 fu-key [^Cells cd ^I32 mode ^I32 r ^I32 k]
  (if (== mode 0)
    (do (if (== k 0) (return (cd-get cd r 2)))
        (if (== k 1) (return (cd-get cd r 6)))
        (if (== k 2) (return (cd-get cd r 5)))
        (if (== k 3) (return (cd-get cd r 3)))
        (return (cd-get cd r 1))))
  (if (== mode 1)
    (do (if (== k 0) (return (cd-get cd r 8)))
        (if (== k 1) (return (cd-get cd r 1)))
        (return 0)))
  (if (== k 0) (return (cd-get cd r 2)))
  (if (== k 1) (return (quot (+ (cd-get cd r 14) 25) 50)))
  (if (== k 2) (return (cd-get cd r 3)))
  (if (== k 3) (return (cd-get cd r 1)))
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 fu-before [^Cells cd ^I32 mode ^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (comment "1 when row a sorts before row b: lexicographic on the mode's five keys, then the row (a total order).")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y 0]
    (while (< k 5)
      (do (set x (fu-key cd mode a k))
          (set y (fu-key cd mode b k))
          (if (< x y) (return 1))
          (if (> x y) (return 0))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (if (< a b) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-sort [^:mut ^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^I32 mode]
  (comment "Shell sort of the row indices in `ord` (Knuth's gaps).")
  (let [^I32 n (cells-len ord)
        ^:mut ^I32 h 1
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 u 0
        ^:mut ^I32 more 1]
    (while (< h (quot n 3))
      (set h (+ (* h 3) 1)))
    (while (>= h 1)
      (do (set i h)
          (while (< i n)
            (do (set v (cells-at ord i))
                (set j i)
                (set more 1)
                (while (and (>= j h) (== more 1))
                  (do (set u (cells-at ord (- j h)))
                      (if (== (fu-before cd mode v u) 1)
                        (do (cells-set ord j u)
                            (set j (- j h)))
                        (set more 0))))
                (cells-set ord j v)
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set h (quot (- h 1) 3))))
    (return 0)))

;; gr (group rows, GR = 16): 0 first position in `ord`, 1 members, 2 distinct pages, 3 zone, 4 qualified (0/1), 5 kind (1 template,
;; 2 style), 6 the page slot (an ordinal, -1), 7 the embedded slot that follows the page (-1), 8 score, 9 isolated members,
;; 10 members with the tag evidence for, 11 against, 12 varying (1: the members differ beyond the page), 13 slots,
;; 14 the class of each slot, two bits each (1 constant, 2 follows the page, 3 varies), 15 1 when the embedded slot equals the page index.

(defn ^I32 fu-cluster [^:mut ^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^:mut ^Cells gr ^Cells pages ^I32 mode]
  (comment "Sort `ord` by the mode's keys and cut it into groups: a new group where the zone, the hash (mode 0) or the size")
  (comment "(mode 2) change, or the vertical position moves more than FU_YTOL per mille of the page's height from the member")
  (comment "before it. Fills `gr`'s kind, zone, first position and members, and every row's group. Answers the number of groups.")
  (fu-sort ord cd mode)
  (cells-drop gr 0)
  (let [^I32 n (cells-len ord)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g -1
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cut 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tol 0]
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set r (cells-at ord i))
          (set cut 1)
          (if (> i 0)
            (do (set q (cells-at ord (- i 1)))
                (set tol (quot (* (page-h pages (- (cd-get cd r 1) 1)) FU_YTOL) 1000))
                (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) (cd-get cd q 2))
                  (if (== mode 0)
                    (if (and (== (cd-get cd r 5) (cd-get cd q 5)) (== (cd-get cd r 6) (cd-get cd q 6)))
                      (if (<= (- (cd-get cd r 3) (cd-get cd q 3)) tol) (set cut 0)))
                    (if (== (fu-key cd 2 r 1) (fu-key cd 2 q 1))
                      (if (<= (- (cd-get cd r 3) (cd-get cd q 3)) tol) (set cut 0)))))))
          (if (== cut 1)
            (do (set g (fu-push-row gr 16))
                (gr-set gr g 0 i)
                (gr-set gr g 3 (cd-get cd r 2))
                (if (== mode 0)
                  (gr-set gr g 5 1)
                  (gr-set gr g 5 2))
                (gr-set gr g 6 -1)
                (gr-set gr g 7 -1)))
          (gr-inc gr g 1)
          (cd-set cd r 8 g)
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return (quot (cells-len gr) 16))))

(defn ^I32 fu-stats [^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^:mut ^Cells gr]
  (comment "Per group: the distinct pages and the tag evidence for and against, over its members (in page order).")
  (let [^I32 ng (quot (cells-len gr) 16)
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prev 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0]
    (while (< g ng)
      (do (set f (gr-get gr g 0))
          (set m (gr-get gr g 1))
          (set prev -1)
          (gr-set gr g 2 0)
          (gr-set gr g 10 0)
          (gr-set gr g 11 0)
          (set i 0)
          (while (< i m)
            (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
                (if (!= (cd-get cd r 1) prev)
                  (do (gr-inc gr g 2)
                      (set prev (cd-get cd r 1))))
                (if (== (cd-get cd r 9) 1) (gr-inc gr g 10))
                (if (== (cd-get cd r 9) 2) (gr-inc gr g 11))
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set g (+ g 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-iso-count [^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^:mut ^Cells gr]
  (comment "Per group: how many members are isolated (gr 9).")
  (let [^I32 ng (quot (cells-len gr) 16)
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0]
    (while (< g ng)
      (do (set f (gr-get gr g 0))
          (set m (gr-get gr g 1))
          (gr-set gr g 9 0)
          (set i 0)
          (while (< i m)
            (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
                (if (>= (cd-get cd r 10) FU_ISOGAP) (gr-inc gr g 9))
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set g (+ g 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-iso [^Cells ln ^:mut ^Cells cd ^Cells gr ^I32 ncd]
  (comment "Isolation (3): for each candidate, is the nearest other line toward the inside of the page at least half a line")
  (comment "away? The lines that are members of a template group seen on two or more pages do not count: they are the")
  (comment "furniture. A margin line is isolated by definition. Answers 0.")
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 l2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 gap 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cy2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 skip 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rr 0]
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (set p (ln-get ln l (lh-page)))
          (set e l)
          (while (and (< e nl) (== (ln-get ln e (lh-page)) p))
            (set e (+ e 1)))
          (while (and (< r0 ncd) (< (cd-get cd r0 1) p))
            (set r0 (+ r0 1)))
          (set r1 r0)
          (while (and (< r1 ncd) (== (cd-get cd r1 1) p))
            (set r1 (+ r1 1)))
          (set r r0)
          (while (< r r1)
            (do (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 3)
                  (cd-set cd r 10 100000)
                  (do (set y0 (cd-get cd r 3))
                      (set y1 (cd-get cd r 4))
                      (set best 1000000000)
                      (set q r0)
                      (set l2 l)
                      (while (< l2 e)
                        (do (set skip 0)
                            (if (== l2 (cd-get cd r 0)) (set skip 1))
                            (set rot (ln-get ln l2 (lh-rot)))
                            (if (and (>= rot 100) (<= rot 35900)) (set skip 1))
                            (while (and (< q r1) (< (cd-get cd q 0) l2))
                              (set q (+ q 1)))
                            (if (and (< q r1) (== (cd-get cd q 0) l2))
                              (do (set rr (cd-get cd q 8))
                                  (if (>= (gr-get gr rr 2) 2) (set skip 1))))
                            (if (== skip 0)
                              (do (set cy2 (+ (ln-get ln l2 (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln l2 (lh-y1))))
                                  (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 1)
                                    (if (> cy2 (* 2 y1))
                                      (do (set gap (- (ln-get ln l2 (lh-y0)) y1))
                                          (if (< gap best) (set best gap)))))
                                  (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 2)
                                    (if (< cy2 (* 2 y0))
                                      (do (set gap (- y0 (ln-get ln l2 (lh-y1))))
                                          (if (< gap best) (set best gap)))))))
                            (set l2 (+ l2 1))))
                      (set best (fu-min best 1000000))
                      (if (< best -1000000) (set best -1000000))
                      (cd-set cd r 10 (quot (* best 1000) (fu-max 1 (- y1 y0))))))
                (set r (+ r 1))))
          (set r0 r1)
          (set l e)))
    (return 0)))

;; --------------------------------------------------------------- the slots of a group
(defn ^I32 fu-slot-value [^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 j]
  (return (sl-get sl (+ (cd-get cd r 13) j) 2)))

(defn ^I32 fu-slot-kind [^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 j]
  (return (sl-get sl (+ (cd-get cd r 13) j) 1)))

(defn ^I32 fu-class-bit [^I32 j]
  (comment "4 to the j: where the two bits of slot j's class sit in gr 14.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 v 1
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0]
    (while (< i j)
      (do (set v (* v 4))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return v)))

(defn ^I32 fu-analyze [^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^:mut ^Cells gr ^I32 g]
  (comment "Classify each slot of the group's template over its members, in page order: 1 the same on every page, 2 follows")
  (comment "the page (the value steps by the page step in at least FU_PAIRS per cent of consecutive pairs), 3 varies. The first")
  (comment "standalone slot that follows the page is the PAGE SLOT; the first embedded one is the EMBEDDED slot, `exact` (gr 15)")
  (comment "when every pair stepped and its value is the page index. A group varies (gr 12) when a slot varies or an embedded")
  (comment "slot is not exact. Answers 0.")
  (let [^I32 f (gr-get gr g 0)
        ^I32 m (gr-get gr g 1)
        ^I32 rep (cells-at ord f)
        ^I32 ns (cd-get cd rep 7)
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cls 0
        ^:mut ^I32 bits 0
        ^:mut ^I32 same 0
        ^:mut ^I32 npairs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pr 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pv 0
        ^:mut ^I32 kind 0]
    (gr-set gr g 6 -1)
    (gr-set gr g 7 -1)
    (gr-set gr g 12 0)
    (gr-set gr g 13 ns)
    (gr-set gr g 14 0)
    (gr-set gr g 15 0)
    (if (< ns 1) (return 0))
    (while (< j ns)
      (do (set same 1)
          (set npairs 0)
          (set nok 0)
          (set pr rep)
          (set pv (fu-slot-value cd sl rep j))
          (set i 1)
          (while (< i m)
            (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
                (set v (fu-slot-value cd sl r j))
                (if (!= v (fu-slot-value cd sl rep j)) (set same 0))
                (if (!= (cd-get cd r 1) (cd-get cd pr 1))
                  (do (set npairs (+ npairs 1))
                      (if (and (>= v 0) (and (>= pv 0) (== (- v pv) (- (cd-get cd r 1) (cd-get cd pr 1)))))
                        (set nok (+ nok 1)))))
                (set pr r)
                (set pv v)
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set cls 3)
          (if (== same 1) (set cls 1))
          (if (and (== cls 3) (and (>= npairs 1) (>= (* nok 100) (* npairs FU_PAIRS)))) (set cls 2))
          (set kind (fu-slot-kind cd sl rep j))
          (set bits (+ bits (* cls (fu-class-bit j))))
          (if (== cls 3) (gr-set gr g 12 1))
          (if (== cls 2)
            (do (if (and (!= kind 3) (== (gr-get gr g 6) -1))
                  (gr-set gr g 6 j)
                  (if (and (== kind 3) (== (gr-get gr g 7) -1))
                    (do (gr-set gr g 7 j)
                        (if (and (== nok npairs) (== (fu-slot-value cd sl rep j) (cd-get cd rep 1)))
                          (gr-set gr g 15 1)))
                    (gr-set gr g 12 1)))))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (gr-set gr g 14 bits)
    (if (and (>= (gr-get gr g 7) 0) (== (gr-get gr g 15) 0)) (gr-set gr g 12 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-qualify [^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^Cells tx ^:mut ^Cells gr ^I32 g ^I32 npages ^I32 trust]
  (comment "SPEC 10.2 step 1 and D076: does the template group qualify as furniture? The score is the recurrence (300 for one")
  (comment "page, 500 + 150 per page beyond, at most 1000) plus FU_TAGW tenths of `trust` times the share of members that are")
  (comment "tagged artifacts in place minus the share that are tagged content; it needs FU_QUAL, and the coverage (at least")
  (comment "FU_COVER per cent of the pages, or 3 pages for a page number, or the tree's word) and the isolation (at least")
  (comment "FU_ISOPCT per cent of the members, or a page number, or the tree's word). A page number the tree marks Pagination is")
  (comment "taken from one page. Answers 1 or 0 and sets gr 4, 8.")
  (let [^I32 f (gr-get gr g 0)
        ^I32 m (gr-get gr g 1)
        ^I32 c (gr-get gr g 2)
        ^I32 rep (cells-at ord f)
        ^I32 ns (cd-get cd rep 7)
        ^I32 s (quot (* (gr-get gr g 10) 1000) m)
        ^I32 o (quot (* (gr-get gr g 11) 1000) m)
        ^:mut ^I32 er 300
        ^:mut ^I32 score 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pagelike 0
        ^:mut ^I32 covok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 isook 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tag 0]
    (gr-set gr g 4 0)
    (gr-set gr g 8 0)
    (if (< ns 0) (return 0))
    ;; a caption that changes from page to page is content
    (if (and (== (gr-get gr g 12) 1) (== (fu-caption-lead tx cd rep) 1)) (return 0))
    (if (>= c 2) (set er (fu-min 1000 (+ 500 (* 150 c)))))
    (set score (+ er (quot (* (quot (* trust (- s o)) 1000) FU_TAGW) 10)))
    (gr-set gr g 8 (fu-max 0 (fu-min 1000 score)))
    (if (and (>= s 800) (>= trust 300)) (set tag 1))
    (if (>= (gr-get gr g 6) 0) (set pagelike 1))
    (if (>= (* c 100) (* npages FU_COVER)) (set covok 1))
    (if (and (== pagelike 1) (>= c 3)) (set covok 1))
    (if (== tag 1) (set covok 1))
    (if (>= (* (gr-get gr g 9) 100) (* m FU_ISOPCT)) (set isook 1))
    (if (== pagelike 1) (set isook 1))
    (if (== tag 1) (set isook 1))
    (if (== (gr-get gr g 3) 3)
      (do (set covok 0)
          (if (and (>= c 3) (>= (* c 100) (* npages 50))) (set covok 1))))
    (if (and (>= score FU_QUAL) (and (== covok 1) (== isook 1)))
      (do (gr-set gr g 4 1)
          (return 1)))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-chain-adjacent [^Cells ln ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^I32 r]
  (comment "1 when candidate r has, on its page and in its zone, a candidate that qualified (cell 15 is 1) directly toward the page's edge from it: within FU_CHAIN_GAP per mille")
  (comment "of its own height of it, and its left edge within two heights of r's (the first line of a two-line header, over the second). Not a cell of a table's row (FU_CELLS")
  (comment "candidates on its baseline).")
  (let [^I32 lo (fu-max 0 (- r 30))
        ^I32 hi (fu-min ncd (+ r 31))
        ^I32 h (fu-max 1 (- (cd-get cd r 4) (cd-get cd r 3)))
        ^I32 c2 (+ (cd-get cd r 3) (cd-get cd r 4))
        ^:mut ^I32 q lo
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 gap 0]
    (while (< q hi)
      (do (if (and (== (cd-get cd q 1) (cd-get cd r 1))
                   (and (== (cd-get cd q 2) (cd-get cd r 2))
                        (<= (fu-abs (- (+ (cd-get cd q 3) (cd-get cd q 4)) c2)) h)))
            (set n (+ n 1)))
          (set q (+ q 1))))
    (if (>= n FU_CELLS) (return 0))
    (set q lo)
    (while (< q hi)
      (do (if (and (!= q r)
                   (and (== (cd-get cd q 1) (cd-get cd r 1))
                        (and (== (cd-get cd q 2) (cd-get cd r 2))
                             (and (== (cd-get cd q 15) 1)
                                  (<= (fu-abs (- (ln-get ln (cd-get cd q 0) (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln (cd-get cd r 0) (lh-x0)))) (* 2 h))))))
            (do (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 1)
                  (do (set gap (- (cd-get cd r 3) (cd-get cd q 4)))
                      (if (and (>= gap -200) (<= (* gap 1000) (* h FU_CHAIN_GAP)) (< (cd-get cd q 3) (cd-get cd r 3)))
                        (return 1))))
                (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 2)
                  (do (set gap (- (cd-get cd q 3) (cd-get cd r 4)))
                      (if (and (>= gap -200) (<= (* gap 1000) (* h FU_CHAIN_GAP)) (> (cd-get cd q 3) (cd-get cd r 3)))
                        (return 1))))))
          (set q (+ q 1))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-chain [^Cells ln ^Cells ord ^:mut ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^Cells tx ^:mut ^Cells gr ^I32 ng ^I32 ncd ^I32 npages ^I32 trust]
  (comment "D1630 (smoke review B issue 11): a template group that qualified in everything but its isolation, whose every member (at least 70 per cent) lies directly under or over a member of a group that")
  (comment "qualified, on the same page and in the same zone, is the next line of that header or footer: a two-line running header has its second line against the body, and only")
  (comment "the first is set apart (the lines that recur do not count). Qualified groups are marked (cell 15 is 1) so a third line goes with the second. Answers the groups added.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 pass 0
        ^:mut ^I32 changed 1
        ^:mut ^I32 added 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 adj 0
        ^:mut ^I32 old 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0]
    (while (and (== changed 1) (< pass 3))
      (do (set changed 0)
          (set g 0)
          (while (< g ng)
            (do (if (and (== (gr-get gr g 4) 0) (and (>= (gr-get gr g 2) 2) (or (== (gr-get gr g 3) 1) (== (gr-get gr g 3) 2))))
                  (do (set f (gr-get gr g 0))
                      (set m (gr-get gr g 1))
                      (set adj 0)
                      (set i 0)
                      (while (< i m)
                        (do (set adj (+ adj (fu-chain-adjacent ln cd ncd (cells-at ord (+ f i)))))
                            (set i (+ i 1))))
                      (if (>= (* adj 100) (* m 70))
                        (do (set old (gr-get gr g 9))
                            (gr-set gr g 9 m)
                            (if (== (fu-qualify ord cd sl tx gr g npages trust) 1)
                              (do (set i 0)
                                  (while (< i m)
                                    (do (cd-set cd (cells-at ord (+ f i)) 15 1)
                                        (set i (+ i 1))))
                                  (set added (+ added 1))
                                  (set changed 1))
                              (gr-set gr g 9 old))))))
                (set g (+ g 1))))
          (set pass (+ pass 1))))
    (return added)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- normalised text and hashes
(defn ^I32 fu-norm-cp [^I32 c]
  (comment "What a character is in a comparison of titles: a letter or a digit, lowercase; 0 for anything else.")
  (if (== (fu-alnum c) 0) (return 0))
  (return (fu-lower c)))

(defn ^I64 fu-hash-cells [^Cells c ^I32 s ^I32 n]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I64 h (fu-basis)]
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set x (fu-norm-cp (cells-at c (+ s i))))
          (if (> x 0) (set h (fu-step h x)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return h)))

(defn ^I32 fu-norm-len [^Cells c ^I32 s ^I32 n]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0]
    (while (< i n)
      (do (if (> (fu-norm-cp (cells-at c (+ s i))) 0) (set k (+ k 1)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return k)))

(defn ^I64 fu-hash-lines [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^I32 l0 ^I32 k]
  (comment "The hash of the normalised text of k consecutive lines read as one.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 l l0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I64 h (fu-basis)]
    (while (< l (+ l0 k))
      (do (set w 0)
          (while (< w (ln-get ln l (lh-count)))
            (do (set ts (wd-get wd (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-first)) w) (hd-tstart)))
                (set tl (wd-get wd (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-first)) w) (hd-tlen)))
                (if (and (>= ts 0) (> tl 0))
                  (do (set j 0)
                      (while (< j tl)
                        (do (set x (fu-norm-cp (cells-at et (+ ts j))))
                            (if (> x 0) (set h (fu-step h x)))
                            (set j (+ j 1))))))
                (set w (+ w 1))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (return h)))

(defn ^I32 fu-len-lines [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^I32 l0 ^I32 k]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 l l0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0]
    (while (< l (+ l0 k))
      (do (set w 0)
          (while (< w (ln-get ln l (lh-count)))
            (do (set ts (wd-get wd (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-first)) w) (hd-tstart)))
                (set tl (wd-get wd (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-first)) w) (hd-tlen)))
                (if (and (>= ts 0) (> tl 0))
                  (set n (+ n (fu-norm-len et ts tl))))
                (set w (+ w 1))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (return n)))

(defn ^I32 fu-bh-sort [^:mut ^Cells bh]
  (comment "Shell sort of the rows (low, high) of `bh` by (high, low).")
  (let [^I32 n (quot (cells-len bh) 2)
        ^:mut ^I32 h 1
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lo 0
        ^:mut ^I32 hi 0
        ^:mut ^I32 more 1]
    (while (< h (quot n 3))
      (set h (+ (* h 3) 1)))
    (while (>= h 1)
      (do (set i h)
          (while (< i n)
            (do (set lo (cells-at bh (* i 2)))
                (set hi (cells-at bh (+ (* i 2) 1)))
                (set j i)
                (set more 1)
                (while (and (>= j h) (== more 1))
                  (do (if (or (< hi (cells-at bh (+ (* (- j h) 2) 1)))
                              (and (== hi (cells-at bh (+ (* (- j h) 2) 1))) (< lo (cells-at bh (* (- j h) 2)))))
                        (do (cells-set bh (* j 2) (cells-at bh (* (- j h) 2)))
                            (cells-set bh (+ (* j 2) 1) (cells-at bh (+ (* (- j h) 2) 1)))
                            (set j (- j h)))
                        (set more 0))))
                (cells-set bh (* j 2) lo)
                (cells-set bh (+ (* j 2) 1) hi)
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set h (quot (- h 1) 3))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-bh-has [^Cells bh ^I64 h]
  (comment "Is the 64-bit hash one of the rows of the sorted `bh`?")
  (let [^I32 lo (i32 h)
        ^I32 hi (i32 (shr64 h 32))
        ^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 b (quot (cells-len bh) 2)
        ^:mut ^I32 mid 0]
    (while (< a b)
      (do (set mid (quot (+ a b) 2))
          (if (and (== (cells-at bh (* mid 2)) lo) (== (cells-at bh (+ (* mid 2) 1)) hi)) (return 1))
          (if (or (< (cells-at bh (+ (* mid 2) 1)) hi)
                  (and (== (cells-at bh (+ (* mid 2) 1)) hi) (< (cells-at bh (* mid 2)) lo)))
            (set a (+ mid 1))
            (set b mid))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-cd-find [^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^I32 l]
  (comment "The candidate row of line l (candidate rows are in line order), or -1.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 a 0
        ^:mut ^I32 b ncd
        ^:mut ^I32 mid 0]
    (while (< a b)
      (do (set mid (quot (+ a b) 2))
          (if (== (cd-get cd mid 0) l) (return mid))
          (if (< (cd-get cd mid 0) l) (set a (+ mid 1)) (set b mid))))
    (return -1)))

(defn ^I32 fu-body-hashes [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^Cells txt ^Cells md ^:mut ^Cells bh]
  (comment "The hashes of everything the output will say: every line that is not a member of a qualified group, alone and with")
  (comment "the one or two lines after it on the page, and the document's Info /Title, each of at least FU_MINNORM letters and")
  (comment "digits; sorted. A running title that is already one of them is the output saying it twice.")
  (cells-drop bh 0)
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I64 h 0]
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (set p (ln-get ln l (lh-page)))
          (set k 1)
          (set ok 1)
          (while (and (<= k 3) (== ok 1))
            (do (if (>= (+ l (- k 1)) nl)
                  (set ok 0)
                  (do (if (!= (ln-get ln (+ l (- k 1)) (lh-page)) p) (set ok 0))
                      (set q (fu-cd-find cd ncd (+ l (- k 1))))
                      (if (>= q 0) (if (> (cd-get cd q 15) 0) (set ok 0)))))
                (if (== ok 1)
                  (if (>= (fu-len-lines wd ln et l k) FU_MINNORM)
                    (do (set h (fu-hash-lines wd ln et l k))
                        (cells-push bh (i32 h))
                        (cells-push bh (i32 (shr64 h 32))))))
                (set k (+ k 1))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (if (and (> (cells-len md) (+ FU_MD_TITLE 1)) (> (cells-at md (+ FU_MD_TITLE 1)) 0))
      (if (>= (fu-norm-len txt (cells-at md FU_MD_TITLE) (cells-at md (+ FU_MD_TITLE 1))) FU_MINNORM)
        (do (set h (fu-hash-cells txt (cells-at md FU_MD_TITLE) (cells-at md (+ FU_MD_TITLE 1))))
            (cells-push bh (i32 h))
            (cells-push bh (i32 (shr64 h 32))))))
    (fu-bh-sort bh)
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-title-match [^Cells bh ^Cells c ^I32 s ^I32 n]
  (comment "Is the text c[s, s+n) (normalised) something the output already says? At least FU_MINNORM letters and digits.")
  (if (< (fu-norm-len c s n) FU_MINNORM) (return 0))
  (return (fu-bh-has bh (fu-hash-cells c s n))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------- decomposition (SPEC 10.2 step 2)
(defn ^I32 fu-next-tok [^Cells tx ^I32 i ^I32 end ^I32 tok]
  (comment "From i (just after the token numbered `tok`), the next token that is not only punctuation, as its ordinal * 8 + its")
  (comment "class (`fu-tclass`); -1 when there is none.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 p i
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ce 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n (+ tok 1)]
    (while (< p end)
      (if (== (cells-at tx p) 32)
        (set p (+ p 1))
        (do (set e p)
            (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
              (set e (+ e 1)))
            (set cs (fu-cs tx p e))
            (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
            (set k (fu-tclass tx cs ce))
            (if (!= k 0) (return (+ (* n 8) k)))
            (set n (+ n 1))
            (set p e))))
    (return -1)))

(defn ^I32 fu-decomp [^Cells tx ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 pj ^I32 ej ^I32 pad ^:mut ^Cells ft]
  (comment "What REMAINS of candidate r's text once the page numbering is taken out, appended to `ft`; answers its length.")
  (comment "With a PAGE SLOT `pj` (an ordinal among the candidate's slots; -1 none) out go: its token; a page word (`Page`, `Seite`)")
  (comment "next to it; an \"of\" word (`of`, `de`, `von`) before a number, and that number, the total; and the tokens that are only")
  (comment "punctuation. Without one the text is copied as it is. The EMBEDDED slot `ej`, when given, is written as the template `{n}`")
  (comment "(`{n:0W}` when `pad` is the width W of its zero-padded digits) in place of its digits.")
  (let [^I32 bs (cd-get cd r 11)
        ^I32 end (+ bs (cd-get cd r 12))
        ^I32 first (cd-get cd r 13)
        ^I32 start (cells-len ft)
        ^:mut ^I32 pjtok -1
        ^:mut ^I32 ejs -1
        ^:mut ^I32 ejl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i bs
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ce 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nx 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prevslot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prevof 0
        ^:mut ^I32 sepof 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 skip 0
        ^:mut ^I32 started 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (if (>= pj 0) (set pjtok (sl-get sl (+ first pj) 5)))
    (if (>= ej 0)
      (do (set ejs (+ bs (sl-get sl (+ first ej) 3)))
          (set ejl (sl-get sl (+ first ej) 4))))
    (while (< i end)
      (if (== (cells-at tx i) 32)
        (set i (+ i 1))
        (do (set e i)
            (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
              (set e (+ e 1)))
            (set cs (fu-cs tx i e))
            (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
            (set k (fu-tclass tx cs ce))
            (set nx -1)
            (if (>= pj 0) (set nx (fu-next-tok tx e end tok)))
            (set skip 0)
            (if (and (== k 0) (>= pj 0)) (set skip 1))
            (if (== tok pjtok) (set skip 1))
            (if (and (>= pj 0) (== k 1))
              (if (or (== prevslot 1) (and (>= nx 0) (== (quot nx 8) pjtok))) (set skip 1)))
            (if (and (>= pj 0) (== k 2))
              (if (and (>= nx 0) (== (rem nx 8) 3)) (set skip 1)))
            (if (and (>= pj 0) (and (== k 3) (or (== prevof 1) (== sepof 1)))) (set skip 1))
            (if (== skip 0)
              (do (if (== started 1) (cells-push ft 32))
                  (set started 1)
                  (set j i)
                  (while (< j e)
                    (if (and (>= ejs 0) (== j ejs))
                      (do (cells-push ft 123)
                          (cells-push ft 110)
                          (if (> pad 0)
                            (do (cells-push ft 58)
                                (cells-push ft 48)
                                (cells-push ft (+ 48 pad))))
                          (cells-push ft 125)
                          (set j (+ j ejl)))
                      (do (cells-push ft (cells-at tx j))
                          (set j (+ j 1)))))))
            (if (!= k 0)
              (do (set prevslot 0)
                  (if (== tok pjtok) (set prevslot 1))
                  (set prevof 0)
                  (if (and (== k 2) (== skip 1)) (set prevof 1))))
            (if (== k 0)
              (if (and (== (- e i) 1) (== (cells-at tx i) 47)) (set sepof 1))
              (set sepof 0))
            (set tok (+ tok 1))
            (set i e))))
    (return (- (cells-len ft) start))))

(defn ^I32 fu-pagenum-slot [^Cells tx ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^I32 r ^I32 lone]
  (comment "For a candidate that is in no template group: the slot of its page number when the line says `page` in so many words")
  (comment "(a page word, and nothing else but numbers, \"of\" words and punctuation: `Seite 12`, `Page iv of x`), or is a number alone")
  (comment "and equal to the page's index (`12` on page 12); else -1.")
  (let [^I32 bs (cd-get cd r 11)
        ^I32 end (+ bs (cd-get cd r 12))
        ^I32 first (cd-get cd r 13)
        ^I32 ns (cd-get cd r 7)
        ^:mut ^I32 i bs
        ^:mut ^I32 e 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ce 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 words 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ntok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0]
    (if (< ns 1) (return -1))
    (while (< i end)
      (if (== (cells-at tx i) 32)
        (set i (+ i 1))
        (do (set e i)
            (while (and (< e end) (!= (cells-at tx e) 32))
              (set e (+ e 1)))
            (set cs (fu-cs tx i e))
            (set ce (fu-ce tx cs e))
            (set k (fu-tclass tx cs ce))
            (if (and (== k 5) (< (fu-prefixed tx cs ce) 0)) (return -1))
            (if (== k 1) (set words (+ words 1)))
            (if (!= k 0) (set ntok (+ ntok 1)))
            (set i e))))
    (if (== words 0)
      (do (if (and (== ntok 1) (== lone 1) (!= (sl-get sl first 1) 3)) (return 0))
          (if (and (== ntok 1) (and (== (sl-get sl first 1) 1) (== (sl-get sl first 2) (cd-get cd r 1))))
            (return 0))
          (if (and (== ntok 1) (== (sl-get sl first 1) 4)) (return 0))
          (return -1)))
    (while (< j ns)
      (do (if (!= (sl-get sl (+ first j) 1) 3) (return j))
          (set j (+ j 1))))
    (return -1)))

(defn ^I32 fu-pad [^Cells ord ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^Cells gr ^I32 g ^I32 ej]
  (comment "The width W of a zero-padded embedded number (`ACME-01`): every member has W digits and some value is shorter")
  (comment "than W digits; else 0 (the template is `{n}`).")
  (let [^I32 f (gr-get gr g 0)
        ^I32 m (gr-get gr g 1)
        ^I32 w (sl-get sl (+ (cd-get cd (cells-at ord f) 13) ej) 6)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 lim 1
        ^:mut ^I32 padded 0
        ^:mut ^I32 s 0]
    (if (or (< w 2) (> w 9)) (return 0))
    (while (< (+ i 1) w)
      (do (set lim (* lim 10))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i m)
      (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
          (set s (+ (cd-get cd r 13) ej))
          (if (!= (sl-get sl s 6) w) (return 0))
          (if (< (sl-get sl s 2) lim) (set padded 1))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (if (== padded 1) (return w))
    (return 0)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------- the outcomes
;; fo (FO = 12): 0 kind (1 ledger row, 2 furniture), then for 1: 1 reason, 2 page, 3-6 box, 7 conf, 8 src, 9 text start in `ft`,
;; 10 text length; for 2: 1 role, 2 conf, 3 src, 4 template start in `ft`, 5 its length, 6 first row in `fp`, 7 rows.
;; fp (FP = 5): page, x0, y0, x1, y1. pl (3 per page): the best label's score, start in `ft`, length.

(defn ^I32 fu-out-ledger [^:mut ^Cells fo ^I32 reason ^I32 page ^I32 x0 ^I32 y0 ^I32 x1 ^I32 y1 ^I32 conf ^I32 src ^I32 ts ^I32 tl]
  (let [^I32 r (fu-push-row fo 12)]
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 0) 1)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 1) reason)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 2) page)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 3) x0)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 4) y0)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 5) x1)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 6) y1)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 7) conf)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 8) src)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 9) ts)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 10) tl)
    (return r)))

(defn ^I32 fu-out-furniture [^:mut ^Cells fo ^I32 role ^I32 conf ^I32 src ^I32 ts ^I32 tl ^I32 f0 ^I32 cnt]
  (let [^I32 r (fu-push-row fo 12)]
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 0) 2)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 1) role)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 2) conf)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 3) src)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 4) ts)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 5) tl)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 6) f0)
    (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 7) cnt)
    (return r)))

(defn ^I32 fu-fp-push [^:mut ^Cells fp ^I32 page ^I32 x0 ^I32 y0 ^I32 x1 ^I32 y1]
  (cells-push fp page)
  (cells-push fp x0)
  (cells-push fp y0)
  (cells-push fp x1)
  (cells-push fp y1)
  (return 0))

(defn ^I32 fu-copy [^Cells src ^I32 s ^I32 n ^:mut ^Cells ft]
  (comment "Append src[s, s+n) to `ft`; answer where it starts.")
  (let [^I32 at (cells-len ft)
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0]
    (while (< i n)
      (do (cells-push ft (cells-at src (+ s i)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return at)))

(defn ^I32 fu-label [^:mut ^Cells pl ^I32 page ^I32 score ^I32 ts ^I32 tl]
  (comment "Offer a page's label; the best score keeps it, the first of equals.")
  (let [^I32 at (* (- page 1) 3)]
    (if (> score (cells-at pl at))
      (do (cells-set pl at score)
          (cells-set pl (+ at 1) ts)
          (cells-set pl (+ at 2) tl)))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-role [^I32 zone]
  (if (== zone 1) (return (rl-header)))
  (if (== zone 2) (return (rl-footer)))
  (return (rl-margin)))

(defn ^I32 fu-emit-group [^Cells ln ^:mut ^Cells cd ^Cells sl ^Cells gr ^Cells ord ^Cells tx ^Cells bh
                          ^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells fp ^:mut ^Cells ft ^:mut ^Cells pl ^I32 g ^I32 mode]
  (comment "Decide a qualified group (SPEC 10.2 step 3) and write the outcomes: per member the page label and the ledger rows,")
  (comment "and the furniture rows. A template group whose members are the same beyond the page (not `varying`) is one furniture")
  (comment "row for all of them; a style group, or a group with a varying slot, is decomposed member by member. `mode` 2 drops what")
  (comment "policy would keep (a `running-title` row says so). Marks the members' lines for removal (cd 15). Answers 0.")
  (let [^I32 f (gr-get gr g 0)
        ^I32 m (gr-get gr g 1)
        ^I32 rep (cells-at ord f)
        ^I32 kind (gr-get gr g 5)
        ^I32 pj (gr-get gr g 6)
        ^I32 ej (gr-get gr g 7)
        ^I32 varying (gr-get gr g 12)
        ^I32 score (gr-get gr g 8)
        ^I32 role (fu-role (gr-get gr g 3))
        ^:mut ^I32 src (+ (sr-text) (sr-infer))
        ^:mut ^I32 rs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tm 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mrs 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mrl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mtm 0
        ^:mut ^I32 mpj 0
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 page 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y1 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ds 0
        ^:mut ^I32 dl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 pad 0
        ^:mut ^I32 usej 0]
    (if (> (gr-get gr g 10) 0) (set src (+ src (sr-struct))))
    (if (and (== kind 1) (== varying 0))
      (do (set rs (cells-len ft))
          (set rl (fu-decomp tx cd sl rep pj -1 0 ft))
          (if (> rl 0) (set tm (fu-title-match bh ft rs rl)))))
    (while (< i m)
      (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
          (if (== (cd-get cd r 15) 0)
            (do (set l (cd-get cd r 0))
                (set page (cd-get cd r 1))
                (set x0 (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)))
                (set y0 (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)))
                (set x1 (ln-get ln l (lh-x1)))
                (set y1 (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)))
                (if (== kind 1)
                  (set mpj pj)
                  (set mpj (fu-pagenum-slot tx cd sl r 0)))
                (if (and (== kind 1) (== varying 0))
                  (do (set mrs rs) (set mrl rl) (set mtm tm))
                  (do (set mrs (cells-len ft))
                      (set mrl (fu-decomp tx cd sl r mpj -1 0 ft))
                      (set mtm 0)
                      (if (> mrl 0) (set mtm (fu-title-match bh ft mrs mrl)))))
                (if (>= mpj 0)
                  (do (set ds (+ (cd-get cd r 11) (sl-get sl (+ (cd-get cd r 13) mpj) 3)))
                      (set dl (sl-get sl (+ (cd-get cd r 13) mpj) 4))
                      (set ts (fu-copy tx ds dl ft))
                      (fu-label pl page score ts dl)
                      (if (== mrl 0)
                        (fu-out-ledger fo (dr-page-number) page x0 y0 x1 y1 score src
                                       (fu-copy tx (cd-get cd r 11) (cd-get cd r 12) ft) (cd-get cd r 12))
                        (fu-out-ledger fo (dr-page-number) page x0 y0 x1 y1 score src ts dl)))
                  (if (== mrl 0)
                    (fu-out-ledger fo (dr-running-title) page x0 y0 x1 y1 score src
                                   (fu-copy tx (cd-get cd r 11) (cd-get cd r 12) ft) (cd-get cd r 12))))
                (if (> mrl 0)
                  (if (or (== mtm 1) (== mode 2))
                    (fu-out-ledger fo (dr-running-title) page x0 y0 x1 y1 score src mrs mrl)
                    (if (or (== varying 1) (== kind 2))
                      (do (set f0 (quot (cells-len fp) 5))
                          (fu-fp-push fp page x0 y0 x1 y1)
                          (fu-out-furniture fo role score src mrs mrl f0 1)))))
                (cd-set cd r 15 kind)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    ;; the same on every page: one furniture row
    (if (and (== kind 1) (and (== varying 0) (and (> rl 0) (and (== tm 0) (!= mode 2)))))
      (do (if (and (>= ej 0) (== (gr-get gr g 15) 1))
            (do (set usej ej)
                (set pad (fu-pad ord cd sl gr g ej)))
            (set usej -1))
          (set ts (cells-len ft))
          (let [^I32 tl (fu-decomp tx cd sl rep pj usej pad ft)]
            (set f0 (quot (cells-len fp) 5))
            (set i 0)
            (while (< i m)
              (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
                  (set l (cd-get cd r 0))
                  (fu-fp-push fp (cd-get cd r 1) (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-x1)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)))
                  (set i (+ i 1))))
            (fu-out-furniture fo role score src ts tl f0 m))))
    (return 0)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------- the style groups
(defn ^I32 fu-sort-nums [^:mut ^Cells c]
  (comment "Shell sort of the numbers in `c`, ascending.")
  (let [^I32 n (cells-len c)
        ^:mut ^I32 h 1
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 u 0
        ^:mut ^I32 more 1]
    (while (< h (quot n 3))
      (set h (+ (* h 3) 1)))
    (while (>= h 1)
      (do (set i h)
          (while (< i n)
            (do (set v (cells-at c i))
                (set j i)
                (set more 1)
                (while (and (>= j h) (== more 1))
                  (do (set u (cells-at c (- j h)))
                      (if (< v u)
                        (do (cells-set c j u)
                            (set j (- j h)))
                        (set more 0))))
                (cells-set c j v)
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set h (quot (- h 1) 3))))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-body-size [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^:mut ^Cells bh]
  (comment "The most common size (to a fifth of a point) of the first word of the lines that are not candidates: the body text's.")
  (comment "0 when there is none. `bh` is scratch.")
  (cells-drop bh 0)
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 best 0
        ^:mut ^I32 bestn 0
        ^:mut ^I32 run 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w0 0]
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (if (>= (ln-get ln l (lh-count)) 1)
            (do (set q (fu-cd-find cd ncd l))
                (if (< q 0)
                  (do (set w0 (ln-get ln l (lh-first)))
                      (cells-push bh (quot (wd-get wd w0 (wf-size)) 20))))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (fu-sort-nums bh)
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i (cells-len bh))
      (do (set v (cells-at bh i))
          (if (and (> i 0) (== v (cells-at bh (- i 1))))
            (set run (+ run 1))
            (set run 1))
          (if (> run bestn)
            (do (set bestn run)
                (set best v)))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (cells-drop bh 0)
    (return (* best 20))))

(defn ^I32 fu-style-pass [^Cells wd ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^Cells txt ^Cells md ^:mut ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^Cells sl ^:mut ^Cells gr ^:mut ^Cells ord ^Cells tx ^:mut ^Cells bh
                          ^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells fp ^:mut ^Cells ft ^:mut ^Cells pl ^Cells pages
                          ^I32 npages ^I32 trust ^I32 bsz ^I32 mode]
  (comment "SPEC 10.2's recurrence for running text that VARIES (evidence 6): among the candidates in the tighter bands, groups")
  (comment "of the same size (to half a point) at the same vertical position, on at least FU_SCOVER per cent of the pages and")
  (comment "isolated on FU_SISO per cent of them, no larger than the body text, are furniture whose text changes (a chapter title,")
  (comment "an odd/even pair). Members already taken by a template group count toward the coverage and are left alone. Answers 0.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cy2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ng 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I32 c 0
        ^:mut ^I32 iso 0
        ^:mut ^I32 free 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ok 0
        ^:mut ^I32 con 0
        ^:mut ^I32 capt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 longest 0]
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r ncd)
      (do (set h (page-h pages (- (cd-get cd r 1) 1)))
          (set cy2 (+ (cd-get cd r 3) (cd-get cd r 4)))
          (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 1)
            (if (>= cy2 (quot (* h FU_STOP) 500)) (cd-set cd r 2 0)))
          (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 2)
            (if (<= cy2 (quot (* h FU_SBOT) 500)) (cd-set cd r 2 0)))
          (if (== (cd-get cd r 2) 3) (cd-set cd r 2 0))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    ;; what the output will say, once the tight-band candidates are out of it: a header must not be its own title
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r ncd)
      (do (if (and (> (cd-get cd r 2) 0) (== (cd-get cd r 15) 0)) (cd-set cd r 15 3))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (fu-body-hashes wd ln et cd ncd txt md bh)
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r ncd)
      (do (if (== (cd-get cd r 15) 3) (cd-set cd r 15 0))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (cells-drop ord 0)
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r ncd)
      (do (cells-push ord r)
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (set ng (fu-cluster ord cd gr pages 2))
    (fu-sort ord cd 1)
    (fu-stats ord cd gr)
    (set g 0)
    (while (< g ng)
      (do (if (> (gr-get gr g 3) 0)
            (do (set f (gr-get gr g 0))
                (set m (gr-get gr g 1))
                (set c (gr-get gr g 2))
                (set iso 0)
                (set free 0)
                (set longest 0)
                (set capt 0)
                (set con (gr-get gr g 11))
                (set i 0)
                (while (< i m)
                  (do (set r (cells-at ord (+ f i)))
                      (if (>= (cd-get cd r 10) FU_SISOGAP) (set iso (+ iso 1)))
                      (if (== (cd-get cd r 15) 0) (set free (+ free 1)))
                      (if (> (cd-get cd r 12) longest) (set longest (cd-get cd r 12)))
                      (if (== (fu-caption-lead tx cd r) 1) (set capt (+ capt 1)))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))
                (set ok 1)
                (if (< c 2) (set ok 0))
                (if (< (* c 100) (* npages FU_SCOVER)) (set ok 0))
                ;; a one-page document has no recurrence to find: a small isolated line in the tight band is a footer or a header
                (if (and (== npages 1) (and (> bsz 0) (<= (* (cd-get cd (cells-at ord f) 14) 100) (* bsz 95)))) (set ok 1))
                (if (< (* iso 100) (* m FU_SISO)) (set ok 0))
                (if (== free 0) (set ok 0))
                (if (> longest FU_SPCLEN) (set ok 0))
                (if (>= (* capt 2) m) (set ok 0))
                (if (and (> bsz 0) (> (mul64 (i64 (cd-get cd (cells-at ord f) 14)) (i64 100)) (mul64 (i64 bsz) (i64 103)))) (set ok 0))
                (if (and (>= trust 500) (>= (* con 1000) (* m 800))) (set ok 0))
                (if (== ok 1)
                  (do (gr-set gr g 4 1)
                      (gr-set gr g 8 (fu-min 1000 (+ 500 (* 100 c))))
                      (gr-set gr g 12 1)
                      (gr-set gr g 6 -1)
                      (gr-set gr g 7 -1)
                      (fu-emit-group ln cd sl gr ord tx bh fo fp ft pl g mode)))))
          (set g (+ g 1))))
    (return 0)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------ the driver
(defn ^I32 fu-watermarks [^Cells wd ^:mut ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^I32 npages ^I32 bsz ^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells ft]
  (comment "Large text set on the diagonal (at least 3 degrees off every right angle) and at least two and a half times the body")
  (comment "size, a few words long: a watermark (`DRAFT`, `CONFIDENTIAL`). It is not content: it is taken out of the flow and the")
  (comment "ledger says `watermark`. (Visibility and the tree's /Watermark artifacts, P3.5-P3.7, are the sharper evidence; this is")
  (comment "the geometry.) Answers the number of lines taken.")
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 dev 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 taken 0]
    (if (<= bsz 0) (return 0))
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (set p (ln-get ln l (lh-page)))
          (if (and (>= p 1) (<= p npages))
            (do (set rot (rem (ln-get ln l (lh-rot)) 9000))
                (set dev rot)
                (if (> (- 9000 rot) 0) (if (< (- 9000 rot) dev) (set dev (- 9000 rot))))
                (set w0 (ln-get ln l (lh-first)))
                (if (and (>= dev 300) (and (>= (ln-get ln l (lh-count)) 1) (<= (ln-get ln l (lh-count)) 4)))
                  (if (>= (* (wd-get wd w0 (wf-size)) 100) (* bsz 250))
                    (do (set ts (cells-len ft))
                        (set tl (fu-line-text wd ln et ft l))
                        (if (and (> tl 0) (<= tl 40))
                          (do (fu-out-ledger fo (dr-watermark) p (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y0))
                                             (ln-get ln l (lh-x1)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)) 600 (+ (sr-text) (sr-infer)) ts tl)
                              (ln-set ln l (lh-page) -7)
                              (set taken (+ taken 1)))
                          (cells-drop ft ts)))))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (return taken)))

(defn ^I32 fu-stamps [^Cells wd ^:mut ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^Cells pages ^I32 npages ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd ^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells fp ^:mut ^Cells ft]
  (comment "D1630 (smoke review B issue 9): a line set sideways (a quarter turn either way) in the outer FU_STAMP per mille of its page's width, at least FU_STAMPLEN characters, is a margin")
  (comment "stamp (the arXiv identifier up the left edge of a paper's first page, a Bates number up a court filing's side): furniture of its own, kept once as a `margin` root whatever the")
  (comment "number of pages it is on (those on several are template groups before this). Taken out of the flow. Answers the lines taken.")
  (let [^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 rot 0
        ^:mut ^I32 w 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cx2 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 taken 0]
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (set p (ln-get ln l (lh-page)))
          (set q (fu-cd-find cd ncd l))
          (if (and (>= p 1) (<= p npages) (or (< q 0) (== (cd-get cd q 15) 0)))
            (do (set rot (ln-get ln l (lh-rot)))
                (if (or (< (fu-abs (- rot 9000)) 100) (< (fu-abs (- rot 27000)) 100))
                  (do (set w (page-w pages (- p 1)))
                      (set cx2 (+ (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-x1))))
                      (if (or (< (* cx2 500) (* w FU_STAMP)) (> (* cx2 500) (* w (- 1000 FU_STAMP))))
                        (do (set ts (cells-len ft))
                            (set tl (fu-line-text wd ln et ft l))
                            (if (and (>= tl FU_STAMPLEN) (<= tl FU_MAXLEN))
                              (do (set f0 (quot (cells-len fp) 5))
                                  (fu-fp-push fp p (ln-get ln l (lh-x0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y0)) (ln-get ln l (lh-x1)) (ln-get ln l (lh-y1)))
                                  (fu-out-furniture fo (rl-margin) 600 (+ (sr-text) (sr-infer)) ts tl f0 1)
                                  (ln-set ln l (lh-page) -7)
                                  (set taken (+ taken 1)))
                              (cells-drop ft ts))))))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (return taken)))

(defn ^I32 fu-fo-key [^Cells fo ^Cells fp ^I32 r ^I32 k]
  (if (== k 0) (return (fo-get fo r 9)))
  (if (== k 1) (return (fo-get fo r 8)))
  (if (== k 2) (return (fo-get fo r 1)))
  (return (cells-at fp (* (fo-get fo r 6) 5))))

(defn ^I32 fu-fo-before [^Cells fo ^Cells fp ^I32 a ^I32 b]
  (let [^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 x 0
        ^:mut ^I32 y 0]
    (while (< k 4)
      (do (set x (fu-fo-key fo fp a k))
          (set y (fu-fo-key fo fp b k))
          (if (< x y) (return 1))
          (if (> x y) (return 0))
          (set k (+ k 1))))
    (if (< a b) (return 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-merge-furniture [^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells fp ^Cells ft ^:mut ^Cells ord]
  (comment "Furniture kept once is kept ONCE (SPEC 10.2): rows with the same role and the same text, found on different pages or")
  (comment "at different heights, become one row whose pages and regions are all of theirs, in page order. `ord` is scratch.")
  (cells-drop ord 0)
  (let [^I32 nr (quot (cells-len fo) 12)
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 h 1
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0
        ^:mut ^I32 u 0
        ^:mut ^I32 more 1
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 tl 0
        ^:mut ^I32 first 0
        ^:mut ^I32 t 0
        ^:mut ^I32 cnt 0
        ^:mut ^I32 f0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 m 0
        ^:mut ^I64 hh 0]
    (while (< r nr)
      (do (if (== (fo-get fo r 0) 2)
            (do (set ts (fo-get fo r 4))
                (set tl (fo-get fo r 5))
                (set hh (fu-basis))
                (set i 0)
                (while (< i tl)
                  (do (set hh (fu-step hh (cells-at ft (+ ts i))))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))
                (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 8) (i32 hh))
                (cells-set fo (+ (* r 12) 9) (i32 (shr64 hh 32)))
                (cells-push ord r)))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (set n (cells-len ord))
    (if (< n 2) (return 0))
    (while (< h (quot n 3))
      (set h (+ (* h 3) 1)))
    (while (>= h 1)
      (do (set i h)
          (while (< i n)
            (do (set v (cells-at ord i))
                (set j i)
                (set more 1)
                (while (and (>= j h) (== more 1))
                  (do (set u (cells-at ord (- j h)))
                      (if (== (fu-fo-before fo fp v u) 1)
                        (do (cells-set ord j u)
                            (set j (- j h)))
                        (set more 0))))
                (cells-set ord j v)
                (set i (+ i 1))))
          (set h (quot (- h 1) 3))))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i n)
      (do (set first (cells-at ord i))
          (set j (+ i 1))
          (while (and (< j n) (and (== (fo-get fo (cells-at ord j) 8) (fo-get fo first 8))
                                    (and (== (fo-get fo (cells-at ord j) 9) (fo-get fo first 9))
                                         (and (== (fo-get fo (cells-at ord j) 1) (fo-get fo first 1))
                                              (== (fo-get fo (cells-at ord j) 5) (fo-get fo first 5))))))
            (set j (+ j 1)))
          (if (> (- j i) 1)
            (do (set f0 (quot (cells-len fp) 5))
                (set cnt 0)
                (set t i)
                (while (< t j)
                  (do (set r (cells-at ord t))
                      (set m 0)
                      (while (< m (fo-get fo r 7))
                        (do (fu-fp-push fp (cells-at fp (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) m) 5))
                                        (cells-at fp (+ (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) m) 5) 1))
                                        (cells-at fp (+ (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) m) 5) 2))
                                        (cells-at fp (+ (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) m) 5) 3))
                                        (cells-at fp (+ (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) m) 5) 4)))
                            (set cnt (+ cnt 1))
                            (set m (+ m 1))))
                      (if (> t i) (cells-set fo (* r 12) 0))
                      (set t (+ t 1))))
                (cells-set fo (+ (* first 12) 6) f0)
                (cells-set fo (+ (* first 12) 7) cnt)))
          (set i j)))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^I32 fu-compact [^:mut ^Cells ln ^Cells cd ^I32 ncd]
  (comment "Take the lines of every candidate that was taken (cd 15 not 0) out of `ln`, keeping the order of the rest.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nl (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 j 0
        ^:mut ^I32 k 0
        ^:mut ^I32 v 0]
    (while (< r ncd)
      (do (if (> (cd-get cd r 15) 0)
            (ln-set ln (cd-get cd r 0) (lh-page) -7))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    (while (< l nl)
      (do (if (!= (ln-get ln l (lh-page)) -7)
            (do (if (!= j l)
                  (do (set k 0)
                      (while (< k 16)
                        (do (set v (ln-get ln l k))
                            (ln-set ln j k v)
                            (set k (+ k 1))))))
                (set j (+ j 1))))
          (set l (+ l 1))))
    (cells-drop ln (* j 16))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 fu-find [^Cells wd ^:mut ^Cells ln ^Cells et ^Cells gl ^Cells mk ^Cells pages ^I32 npages
                          ^Cells txt ^Cells md ^Cells lb ^I32 trust ^I32 mode
                          ^:mut ^Cells cd ^:mut ^Cells sl ^:mut ^Cells gr ^:mut ^Cells ord ^:mut ^Cells tx ^:mut ^Cells bh
                          ^:mut ^Cells fo ^:mut ^Cells fp ^:mut ^Cells ft ^:mut ^Cells pl]
  (comment "Find the running furniture of the document, take its lines out of `ln`, and leave the decisions in `fo fp ft pl` for")
  (comment "`fu-write` (see the head of this file). `txt md lb` are P3.9's (`md` and `lb` empty when it did not run), `trust` the")
  (comment "tagged tree's score (0 when there is none), `mode` 0 policy, 1 keep, 2 skip. All the other arenas are scratch or output,")
  (comment "cleared here. Answers the number of lines taken out of `ln`.")
  (cells-drop cd 0)
  (cells-drop sl 0)
  (cells-drop gr 0)
  (cells-drop ord 0)
  (cells-drop tx 0)
  (cells-drop bh 0)
  (cells-drop fo 0)
  (cells-drop fp 0)
  (cells-drop ft 0)
  (cells-drop pl 0)
  (let [^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ng 0
        ^:mut ^I32 g 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 before (ln-count ln)
        ^:mut ^I32 bsz 0
        ^:mut ^I32 ts 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nn 0]
    (while (< p npages)
      (do (cells-push pl 0)
          (cells-push pl -1)
          (cells-push pl 0)
          (set p (+ p 1))))
    ;; /PageLabels, when the catalogue has them, wins over every printed number (SPEC 10.2)
    (if (and (> (cells-len md) FU_MD_RANGES) (> (cells-at md FU_MD_RANGES) 0))
      (do (set p 0)
          (while (< p npages)
            (do (set ts (cells-len ft))
                (set nn (pm-label-cells txt lb p ft))
                (if (> nn 0) (fu-label pl (+ p 1) 5000 ts nn))
                (set p (+ p 1))))))
    (if (== mode 1) (return 0))
    (set n (fu-scan wd ln et gl mk pages npages cd sl tx))
    (if (< n 0) (return 0))
    (if (>= n 1)
      (do (set r 0)
          (while (< r n)
            (do (cells-push ord r)
                (set r (+ r 1))))
          (set ng (fu-cluster ord cd gr pages 0))
          (fu-sort ord cd 1)
          (fu-stats ord cd gr)
          (fu-iso ln cd gr n)
          (fu-iso-count ord cd gr)
          (set g 0)
          (while (< g ng)
            (do (fu-analyze ord cd sl gr g)
                ;; one page, and the tree says it is in place: its page number, when the line has the shape of one
                (if (and (== (gr-get gr g 2) 1) (and (>= trust 300) (>= (* (gr-get gr g 10) 1000) (* (gr-get gr g 1) 800))))
                  (do (set r (cells-at ord (gr-get gr g 0)))
                      (set nn (fu-pagenum-slot tx cd sl r 1))
                      (gr-set gr g 6 nn)))
                (fu-qualify ord cd sl tx gr g npages trust)
                (if (== (gr-get gr g 4) 1)
                  (do (set r 0)
                      (while (< r (gr-get gr g 1))
                        (do (cd-set cd (cells-at ord (+ (gr-get gr g 0) r)) 15 1)
                            (set r (+ r 1))))))
                (set g (+ g 1))))
          (fu-chain ln ord cd sl tx gr ng n npages trust)
          (fu-body-hashes wd ln et cd n txt md bh)
          ;; the groups that qualified were marked 1 for the body hashes; the emission marks them for removal itself
          (set r 0)
          (while (< r n)
            (do (if (== (cd-get cd r 15) 1) (cd-set cd r 15 0))
                (set r (+ r 1))))
          (set g 0)
          (while (< g ng)
            (do (if (== (gr-get gr g 4) 1)
                  (fu-emit-group ln cd sl gr ord tx bh fo fp ft pl g mode))
                (set g (+ g 1))))))
    (set bsz (fu-body-size wd ln cd n bh))
    (if (>= n 1)
      (fu-style-pass wd ln et txt md cd n sl gr ord tx bh fo fp ft pl pages npages trust bsz mode))
    (fu-watermarks wd ln et npages bsz fo ft)
    (if (== mode 0) (fu-stamps wd ln et pages npages cd n fo fp ft))
    (fu-merge-furniture fo fp ft ord)
    (fu-compact ln cd n)
    (return (- before (ln-count ln)))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------ into the Model
(defn ^:pub ^I32 fu-write [^Cells fo ^Cells fp ^Cells ft ^Cells pl ^I32 npages
                           ^:mut ^Cells nodes ^:mut ^Cells attrs ^:mut ^Cells regions ^:mut ^Cells text
                           ^:mut ^Cells pages ^:mut ^Cells ledger ^:mut ^Cells tmp]
  (comment "Write what `fu-find` decided into the Model, after the paragraph stage: each page's label (page table), the")
  (comment "ledger rows, the `furniture` roots (parent -1: kept once, not in the flow) and the `label` of every `break`")
  (comment "milestone. The text goes through NFC and the ligature fold like every other text (SPEC 3.6). Answers 0.")
  (let [^:mut ^I32 p 0
        ^:mut ^I32 r 0
        ^:mut ^I32 t0 0
        ^:mut ^I32 n 0
        ^:mut ^I32 l 0
        ^:mut ^I32 i 0
        ^:mut ^I32 q 0
        ^:mut ^I32 prevpage 0
        ^:mut ^I32 nf 0]
    (while (< p npages)
      (do (if (and (> (cells-at pl (* p 3)) 0) (> (cells-at pl (+ (* p 3) 2)) 0))
            (do (set t0 (cells-len text))
                (set i 0)
                (while (< i (cells-at pl (+ (* p 3) 2)))
                  (do (text-append-cp text (cells-at ft (+ (cells-at pl (+ (* p 3) 1)) i)))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))
                (page-set-label pages p t0 (cells-at pl (+ (* p 3) 2)))))
          (set p (+ p 1))))
    (set r 0)
    (while (< r (quot (cells-len fo) 12))
      (do (if (== (fo-get fo r 0) 1)
            (do (set l (ledger-add ledger (fo-get fo r 1) (fo-get fo r 2) (fo-get fo r 3) (fo-get fo r 4)
                                   (fo-get fo r 5) (fo-get fo r 6) (fo-get fo r 7) (fo-get fo r 8)))
                (set t0 (cells-len text))
                (nz-nfc ft (fo-get fo r 9) (+ (fo-get fo r 9) (fo-get fo r 10)) text tmp (+ (nz-flag-ligatures) (nz-flag-radicals)))
                (ledger-set-text ledger l t0 (- (cells-len text) t0))))
          (if (== (fo-get fo r 0) 2)
            (do (set nf (node-new nodes (nk-furniture) -1))
                (node-set-sub nodes nf (fo-get fo r 1))
                (set t0 (cells-len text))
                (nz-nfc ft (fo-get fo r 4) (+ (fo-get fo r 4) (fo-get fo r 5)) text tmp (+ (nz-flag-ligatures) (nz-flag-radicals)))
                (node-set-text nodes nf t0 (- (cells-len text) t0))
                (node-set-conf nodes nf (fo-get fo r 2))
                (node-add-src nodes nf (fo-get fo r 3))
                (set prevpage 0)
                (set i 0)
                (while (< i (fo-get fo r 7))
                  (do (set q (* (+ (fo-get fo r 6) i) 5))
                      (node-add-region nodes regions nf (cells-at fp q) (cells-at fp (+ q 1)) (cells-at fp (+ q 2))
                                       (cells-at fp (+ q 3)) (cells-at fp (+ q 4)))
                      (if (!= (cells-at fp q) prevpage)
                        (do (node-add-attr-int nodes attrs nf (fk-pages) (cells-at fp q))
                            (set prevpage (cells-at fp q))))
                      (set i (+ i 1))))))
          (set r (+ r 1))))
    ;; the printed label of every page milestone
    (set n (node-count nodes))
    (set i 0)
    (while (< i n)
      (do (if (== (node-kind nodes i) (nk-break))
            (do (set p (node-sub nodes i))
                (if (and (>= p 1) (<= p (page-count pages)))
                  (if (> (page-label-len pages (- p 1)) 0)
                    (node-set-attr-text nodes attrs i (fk-label) (page-label-start pages (- p 1)) (page-label-len pages (- p 1)))))))
          (set i (+ i 1))))
    (return 0)))
